# Outside Zinc's contract (decided 2026-10-09, may be revisited): a macro may observe any type,
# not only its type arguments, and anything about it beyond the public API. Zinc records a
# macro-expansion dependency on the type arguments and invalidates on their API changes only, so
# a private member the macro lists is not tracked. Use a clean build, or recompileOnMacroDef.
> app/run true

# A loses a private member, which is not part of its API. The macro in W reads it, so W must
# recompile, but no API change is detected.
$ copy-file app/changes/A.scala app/A.scala
> app/run false
